  "text": "# Profiling, labor_mc3units: three labor montecarlo units in one process, on\n# master, the reference for labor_mc3units_gccollect_econfix.\n# Batch 0, rcp85, SSP3, high, with CCSM4, GFDL-ESM2M and MIROC5 run one after\n# another in one process, as a production montecarlo worker does, with the settings of\n# labor/configs/montecarlo/ssp3-rcp85-high.yml.\n# The projection system shuffles the units, so their order may differ\n# between runs. seed-csvv is fixed to the draw of the production labor montecarlo, batch 0, CCSM4\n# (its pvals.yml in /project/cil/gcp/outputs_newsocioeconomics/labor/montecarlo/), so every unit of both\n# versions uses the same coefficients. The histclim year order is a hash of\n# each unit's folder, so it matches between runs too.\n# Outputs go to scratch. The jobs pass\n# --outputdir=/scratch/midway3/$USER/agri-profiling/labor_mc3units/outputs\n# on the command line, so each user writes to their own scratch.\nimport: \"base/uninteracted_main_model.yml\"\nmode: montecarlo\noutputdir: /scratch/midway3/cadavidsanchez/agri-profiling/labor_mc3units/outputs\ntimeout: 12\ndo_farmers: true\ndo_historical: true\nonly-rcp: rcp85\nonly-models: [CCSM4, GFDL-ESM2M, MIROC5]\nonly-ssp: SSP3\nonly-iam: high\nonly-batch-number: 0\npvals:\n  uninteracted_main_model_agnonag_27_28_41:\n    seed-csvv: 100473597000641500511243794462613005915\nsocioeconomic_data_dir: /project/cil/gcp/outputs_newsocioeconomics/socioeconomics/1.0.0/\n"
 },
